<title>UK: UK Treasury agency to take charge of gilt sales.</title>
<headline>UK Treasury agency to take charge of gilt sales.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government announced on Tuesday it was to set up a Treasury agency to implement its previously announced plans to transfer key responsibilities for the management of the gilt markets from the Bank of England.</p>
<p>&quot;We propose to establish an agency of the Treasury to implement the annual borrowing programme, to liaise and deal with participants in the gilts market and to manage the Exchequer's cash position,&quot; financial secretary to the Treasury Helen Liddell said in a written parliamentary reply.</p>
<p>The government said the responsibility would transfer to the Treasury when it announced it was giving the central bank operational control over interest rates.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7767</p>
